{% doc %}
  Emits a conservative responsive `sizes` value for cards in a configurable,
  page-width grid. Grid gaps are intentionally not subtracted so browsers never
  choose an image narrower than the rendered card.

  @param {number} columns - Number of desktop grid columns
  @param {number} [two_column_breakpoint] - Viewport width where the grid changes from one to two columns
  @param {boolean} [full_width] - Set when the grid spans the viewport instead of stopping at the page width

  @example
  {% capture image_sizes %}
    {% render 'grid-image-sizes', columns: section.settings.columns %}
  {% endcapture %}
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign desktop_columns = columns | default: 4
  assign two_column_breakpoint = two_column_breakpoint | default: 550
  assign horizontal_page_margins = settings.min_page_margin | times: 2
-%}

{%- comment -%}
  A grid held to the page width stops growing there, so past it the card is a
  fraction of that fixed width rather than of the viewport — this clause is what
  keeps the browser from over-fetching on a wide monitor.

  A full-width grid never stops, so the same clause would understate the card on
  every screen wider than the page width, and the browser would answer with an
  image too small for it. Leave it out and the `100vw` clause below carries all
  the way up.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- unless full_width -%}
  {%- capture page_width_clause -%}
    (min-width: {{ settings.max_page_width }}) calc(({{ settings.max_page_width }} - {{ horizontal_page_margins }}px) / {{ desktop_columns }}),
  {%- endcapture -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{{- page_width_clause }} (min-width: 990px) calc((100vw - {{ horizontal_page_margins }}px) / {{ desktop_columns }}), (min-width: {{ two_column_breakpoint }}px) calc((100vw - {{ horizontal_page_margins }}px) / 2), calc(100vw - {{ horizontal_page_margins }}px)
